Rast e welle rast e. Dûr e?
 
It's true by God it's true. Is it far?

177
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,000
...wela erê û cihê xwe dîtin...
 
...by God yes, and they found their place...

178
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Lê baş e, berî ku xeta me qut bibe, te behsa çi dikir? Di
nava axaftina xwe de te çi digot?
 
But alright, before our line disconnected, what were you
talking about? In your conversation, what were you saying?

179
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Sûcê me ew e ku tu pereyên xwe didî bajaran. Ez ji gundiyan
re dibêjim, li gundê xwe bixebitin.
 
Our mistake is that you give your money to the cities. I
tell the villagers, work in your own village.

180
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Eger tu li gundê xwe xwedî derkevî, tu dê pereyê xwe winda
nekî û tu yê kirê jî nedî bajaran.
 
If you take care of your village, you won't lose your money
and you won't pay rent to the cities.

181
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:32,000
Naxêr! Ya rastî daxwaza me jî ev e, xortekî mîna we rabe û
projeyekê vebike, daku milet hişyar bibe.
 
No! Actually, our wish is this too, that a young man like
you rises and opens a project, so that the people wake up.

182
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Te digot li nava gund de dikan tune ye...
 
You were saying there are no shops in the village...

183
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Rast e. Noka, di nav gund de dikan tune ye. Eger tu
xizmetekê bînî gund, tu ji bo cîranên xwe jî fêdeyê dikî.
 
That's right. Now, there are no shops in the village. If you
bring a service to the village, you benefit your neighbors
too.

184
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Wate tu ji gundiyan re fêdeyê dikî?
 
Meaning you benefit the villagers?

185
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Belê, tu sûdê digihînî mirovan. Dikan hebe rind e, firne
hebe rind e, berberxane hebe, xeyat hebe rind e.
 
Yes, you benefit people. It's good to have a shop, it's good
to have a bakery, a barbershop, a tailor.

186
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:02,000
Di serî de, xizmetên bi vî rengî li gund gelekî pêwîst in.
 
Above all, services like this are very necessary in the
village.

187
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:10,000
Ev daxwaza me ye, em dixwazin milet rabe. Em bang li xelkê
dikin ku projeyan vekin, tu bi vî karî qet zerar nakî.
 
This is our wish, we want the people to rise. We call on the
people to open projects, you will never lose with this work.

188
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Eger sermayeya te hebe, tu zerar nakî. Wek mînak firneyek,
tu qet pê zerar nakî. Xelk li cem me kom bûn, daxwaz kirin û
me firneyek vekir.
 
If you have capital, you won't lose. For example, a bakery,
you'll never lose on it. People gathered with us, requested
it, and we opened a bakery.

189
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Niha, deh-diwanzdeh gund li dorhêla me ne. Tu dizanî qezenca
rojane ya firneyê çiqas e?
 
Now, there are ten to twelve villages around us. Do you know
how much the daily profit of the bakery is?

190
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Gelek dikişîne yanî?
 
Meaning it draws in a lot?

191
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Dikişîne! Qe nebe rojane heşt sed dolar dertîne.
 
It draws! It makes at least eight hundred dollars a day.

192
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Eger tu xwediyê firneyekê bî û çil-pêncî hezar dolar lê xerc
bikî... lê eger roja te bi heşt sed dolarî be...
 
If you own a bakery and spend forty to fifty thousand
dollars on it... but if your day brings in eight hundred
dollars...

193
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Di mehekê de çiqas kar dibe?
 
How much profit is that in a month?

194
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Di nava du mehan de tu heqê firnê derdixî. Lê li bajêr, tu
cîhekî kirê dikî û rojê pêncî dolar tu didî mesref.
 
Within two months, you make back the cost of the bakery. But
in the city, you rent a place and pay fifty dollars a day in
expenses.

195
00:11:56,000 --> 00:12:02,000
Di mehekê de hezar û pêncsed dolar mesrefa te dibe.
 
In a month, you have one thousand five hundred dollars in
expenses.

196
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:10,000
Lê li gund, ard heye, nan heye, kar rind e. Daxwaza me ev e
ku xelkê me werin projeyên bi vî rengî çêkin.
 
But in the village, there is flour, there is bread, the work
is good. Our wish is for our people to come and build
projects like this.

197
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:20,000
Em dixwazin miletê me şa bibe. Em dixwazin Efrîna xwe şên
bikin û miletê me vegere ser axa xwe. Ji axê şêrîntir tiştek
tune ye.
 
We want our people to be happy. We want to rebuild our Afrin
and have our people return to their land. There is nothing
sweeter than the land.

198
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Wela wekî axê tune ye. Lê tevî vê jî hûn li vir dixebitin,
gundiyên me ne...
 
By God, there is nothing like the land. But despite this,
you work here, you are our villagers...

199
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:33,000
Wela ax e, bê ax jiyan nabe. Em gundî ne û em bi axa xwe ve
girêdayî ne.
 
By God, it's the land, without land there is no life. We are
villagers and we are tied to our land.

200
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Daxwaza we ji xortên li derve çi ye?
 
What is your request to the youth abroad?

201
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Kesên ku li Ewropayê ne, pereyên xwe xistine bankan û
welatên biyanî fêdeyê ji wî pereyî dibînin.
 
The people who are in Europe have put their money in banks,
and foreign countries benefit from that money.

202
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:52,000
Em dibêjin bila wî pereyî bînin vir, li welatê xwe meşrûan
(projeyan) vekin. Dê miletê me hemû sûdê jê werbigire.
 
We say they should bring that money here, and open projects
in their homeland. All our people will benefit from it.

203
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:58,000
Belê, gava her kes projeyekê vebike, gundê wan ava dibe û
xelk jî fêdeyê dibîne.
 
Yes, when everyone opens a project, their village gets
rebuilt and the people benefit.

204
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:04,000
Bêguman. Wê demê herkes dê fêde bibîne û miletê me yê
serbilind be.
 
Absolutely. Then everyone will benefit and our people will
be proud.

205
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Wela, keçên me dixebitin, biçûkên me dixebitin, mêrên me
dixebitin. Ev xebateke pîroz e, xêra we ye.
 
By God, our girls are working, our little ones are working,
our men are working. This is a blessed effort, God reward
you.

206
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Xebat her dem rind e. Seheta gundiyan xweş be, bi hevre kar
dikin.
 
Working is always good. Health to the villagers, they work
together.

207
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Seheta we jî xweş be. Înşallah dengê we digihêje derve jî û
alîkariyê dikin.
 
Health to you too. God willing, your voice reaches abroad
and they help.

208
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Bira, te dît... tişt wekî axa welêt nîne. Ev gundê me ye, em
kurmanc in, em bimirin bimînin li vir in. Ev e halê me.
 
Brother, you see... there is nothing like the homeland's
soil. This is our village, we are Kurds, in life and in
death we are here. This is our situation.

209
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:39,000
Mirin û man li vir e!
 
In life and in death, you are here!

210
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Belê. Ez gundî me, ez naxwazim biçim derve. Welle, eger em
hemû destekê bidin hev, em dikarin gundên xwe baştir bikin.
 
Yes. I am a villager, I don't want to go abroad. By God, if
we all support each other, we can make our villages better.

211
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Wela ramanek gelek baş e. Ev hizreke pir hêja ye ku tu
xizmetê bidî gundê xwe.
 
By God, it's a very good idea. It's a very valuable thought
to serve your village.

212
00:13:55,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Milet ray e, dîtina xelkê heye. Em dibêjin eger her gundiyek
meşrûekê vebike, milet wê rehet be. Em vê daxwaz dikin.
 
The people have a say, the public has views. We say if every
villager opens a project, the people will be at peace. We
request this.

213
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Em daxwaza serkeftinê ji we re dikin. Hûn saet xweş.
 
We wish you success. Health to you.

214
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:16,000
Xwedê we biparêze. Heke pereyê min zêdetir heba min ê
meşrûên hê mezintir vekiribana.
 
May God protect you. If I had more money, I would have
opened even bigger projects.

215
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Xwedê mezin e, înşallah yekî xêrxwaz wê li derve dengê te
bibîhîze.
 
God is great, God willing a benevolent person abroad will
hear your voice.

216
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Înşallah. Ez we dispêrim Xwedê, serkeftin.
 
God willing. I leave you in God's care, success to you.

217
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Spas. Em herin bazara Efrîn, ka em pêşiya xwe binihêrin.
 
Thank you. Let's go to the Afrin market, let's look ahead.

218
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:45,000
(Transition sounds to the market...)
 
(Transition sounds to the market...)

219
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:52,000
Em niha li bazara Efrîn in. Em ê ji xelkê bipirsin ka rewşa
bazarê çawa ye.
 
We are now at the Afrin market. We will ask the people how
the market situation is.

220
00:14:52,000 --> 00:15:00,000
Merheba xalê, em hatine we bibînin. We çawa kir, li bazara
Efrîn as'ar (biha) çawa ne?
 
Hello uncle, we came to see you. How are you doing, how are
the prices at the Afrin market?

221
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Ev sal bihayê heywanan kêm e.
 
This year the price of animals is low.

222
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:10,000
Te berx firotin? As'ar çawa ne îsal?
 
Did you sell lambs? How are the prices this year?

223
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:17,000
As'ar pir nizm in. Me berx anîn, lê xelk pere nîne ku
bikire.
 
Prices are very low. We brought lambs, but the people don't
have money to buy.

224
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:25,000
Yanî kirîn û firotin rawestiyaye? Tu van wek qurbanî
difiroşî, te berxek bi çiqasî firot?
 
So buying and selling has stopped? You're selling these for
sacrifice, how much did you sell a lamb for?

225
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Bi Xwedê, min yek bi 140 dolar firot û yê din bi 120 dolar
firot.
 
By God, I sold one for 140 dollars and another for 120
dollars.

226
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:36,000
Gelo ev heqê mesrefa we derdixe?
 
Does this cover your expenses?

227
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Welleh mesref dernakeve. Alif buha ye, eger em fêdeyekê li
ser nebînin em tenê zerar dikin.
 
By God, it doesn't cover expenses. Feed is expensive, if we
don't see a profit on it, we only suffer a loss.

228
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:49,000
Wezneya (kîloya) van berxan çiqas e?
 
What is the weight of these lambs?

229
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Wezneya wan 20 heta 25 kîlo ne. Em her yekî bi sed û çil yan
sed û bîst dolar difiroşin.
 
Their weight is 20 to 25 kilos. We sell each one for a
hundred and forty or a hundred and twenty dollars.

230
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Milet van rojan mîna qurbanan dikirin?
 
Are people buying these for sacrifice these days?

231
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Belê, yên dixwazin xêrê bikin tên û qurbanekê dikirin. Pênc-
deh kes difiroşin.
 
Yes, those who want to do a good deed come and buy a
sacrifice. Five to ten people sell them.

232
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:15,000
Xwedê xêra wan qebûl bike.
 
May God accept their good deeds.

233
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Lê milet feqîr e. Gelek kes nikarin bikirin.
 
But the people are poor. Many people cannot buy.

234
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Çil yan pêncî berx li cem we hene, hûn di heyvekê de çiqas
mesref dikin?
 
You have forty or fifty lambs with you, how much do you
spend in a month?

235
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Tu heywanekî çar-pênc mehan xwedî dikî, mesrefa alifê gelek
e. Gava tu wî bi 140 dolar difiroşî, qet heqê wê dernakeve.
 
You raise an animal for four to five months, the cost of
feed is a lot. When you sell it for 140 dollars, it doesn't
cover the cost at all.

236
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Eger baran bibariya û alif erzan ba, we qezenc dikir?
 
If it had rained and feed was cheap, would you have made a
profit?

237
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Eger baran hebûya, çêre hebûya, wê mesref kêm ba. Lê îsal
alif buha ye, loma em zerar dikin. Heta em mesrefa wî
derdixin, 150 dolar diçe. Wate em deh dolar zerar dikin.
 
If there was rain, if there was pasture, the cost would have
been lower. But this year feed is expensive, so we lose
money. By the time we cover its cost, it takes 150 dollars.
Meaning we lose ten dollars.

238
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Xwedê arîkarê we be. Hûn xizmet dikin, Xwedê xêra we qebûl
bike.
 
May God help you. You are providing a service, may God
accept your good deeds.

239
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Em mecbûr in bixebitin. Xelk jî qurbanan dikirin bo xêrê, em
jî bi vê razî ne.
 
We are forced to work. The people also buy sacrifices for
charity, and we are content with this.

240
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Serkeftin, em ê herin bal bazirganên din.
 
Success to you, we will go to other merchants.

241
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:22,000
(Host approaches another person)
 
(Host approaches another person)

242
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:27,000
Merheba, xalê. Bazara te çawa ye îro?
 
Hello, uncle. How is your market today?

243
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:33,000
Welleh bazar sist e. Milet hindik e.
 
By God, the market is slow. The people are few.

244
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Te çi anîbû vir? Pez an hesin?
 
What did you bring here? Sheep or iron?

245
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Min pez anî. As'ar nizm e.
 
I brought sheep. Prices are low.

246
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:49,000
Çiqas e as'arê pezî îro li gor weznê?
 
How much are sheep prices today according to weight?

247
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Yê mezin heye bi 150 dolar, yê biçûktir heye bi 100 dolar.
 
There is the large one for 150 dollars, there is the smaller
one for 100 dollars.

248
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Van wek qurban difiroşin?
 
Are they selling these as sacrifices?

249
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Belê qurban in. Kesên dixwazin tên hildibijêrin.
 
Yes, they are sacrifices. Those who want come and choose.

250
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:11,000
Xwedê xêra we binivîse, gelek spas.
 
May God write down your good deeds, thank you very much.

251
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Spas ji we re jî. Saet xweş.
 
Thank you too. Health to you.

252
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Em ê nêrîna xelkê din jî li ser bazarê bigirin... (walks
further)
 
We will get the opinions of other people on the market
too... (walks further)

253
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:29,000
Merheba bira. Te çi dikirî îro?
 
Hello brother. What were you buying today?

254
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:34,000
Min berxek ji bo malê dikirî.
 
I bought a lamb for the house.

255
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:39,000
As'ar çawa bûn li gora te?
 
How were the prices in your opinion?

256
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:45,000
Ji bo miletê me pir buha ye. Pere tune ye di destê xelkê de.
 
For our people it is very expensive. There is no money in
the people's hands.

257
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:49,000
Te bi çendî kirî?
 
How much did you buy it for?

258
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Min bi sed û sih dolarî kirî.
 
I bought it for a hundred and thirty dollars.

259
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:58,000
Tu yê wek qurban ser jê bikî?
 
Will you slaughter it as a sacrifice?

260
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Belê, ji bo qurbanê. Xwedê qebûl bike.
 
Yes, for sacrifice. May God accept it.

261
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Em hêvî dikin Xwedê qebûl bike. Em li bazara Efrîn dibînin
ku kirîn û firotin heye, lê belê milet zehmetiyê dikişîne.
 
We hope God accepts it. We see in the Afrin market that
there is buying and selling, but the people are struggling.

262
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Xelk dixwaze wekî berê bazara Efrîn geş bibe, as'ar ji milet
re guncawtir bin.
 
The people want the Afrin market to flourish like before,
for prices to be more suitable for the people.

263
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:28,000
Helbet bi hevkariyê her tişt baş dibe.
 
Of course, with cooperation everything will be fine.

264
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:35,000
(Background chatter, market sounds)
 
(Background chatter, market sounds)

265
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Em spasiya hemû firoşkar û kiryaran dikin ku bi me re
axivîn.
 
We thank all the sellers and buyers who spoke with us.

266
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Em hêvî dikin rojekê bazara Efrîn û gundên wê dîsa geş û
xweş bibin.
 
We hope one day the Afrin market and its villages will
flourish and become beautiful again.

267
00:19:50,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Heta hevdîtineke din, di bernameyeke din de, em we dispêrin
Xwedê. Bi xatirê we!
 
Until another meeting, in another program, we leave you in
God's care. Goodbye!

268
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Çiqas sal e?
 
(End of Audio Segment)

269
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,000
Çiqas sal e?
 
How many years is it?

270
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Evî ji pêncsed sal e.
 
This is from 500 years ago.

271
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Pêncsed sal?
 
500 years?

272
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Maşelleh gundê me Kurmancan cihê... emrî giyo, gundê giyo
mezin e.
 
Yes, about 500 years.

273
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:09,000
Maşelleh gundê me Kurmancan cihê... emrî giyo, gundê giyo
mezin e.
 
Mashallah, our Kurdish village is a place... its whole age,
the whole village is big.

274
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:12,000
Pêncsed sal avahî ye am zanin. Nexwe ev camiya ha ne ne?
 
We know it is a 500-year-old building. So this is the
mosque, isn't it?

275
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Ev camî kevn e, kel û kelemê kiştiyê nîne.
 
This mosque is old, it doesn't belong to the ship.

276
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Gundê me Kurmancan, camiya emrê xwe hezar sal in ne.
 
Our Kurdish village, its own mosque's age is a thousand
years.

277
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Ka werin em derbasî hundur bin jî.
 
Yes...

278
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Ka werin em derbasî hundur bin jî.
 
Come, let's go inside as well.

279
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Hatina, hatina, hatina, ev du pêre hatine...
 
Go inside.

280
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Hatina, hatina, hatina, ev du pêre hatine...
 
Coming, coming, coming, these two came together...

281
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:27,000
Ev o ev o... ev ê çiye lê?
 
This and this... what is this here?

282
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Dewêr e.
 
It is a mill.

283
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Ev a ne cemê dewêre ye?
 
Isn't this the place of the mill?

284
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Lê.
 
Yes.

285
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:34,000
Tew da... av di kîjanî? Dan... genim?
 
Completely... water in which one? Grain... wheat?

286
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Dan. Erê genim dikutan.. Dan.
 
Grain. Yes, they pounded wheat.. Grain.

287
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:43,000
Ewa... xaltîk dibêje tê de genim dikutan. Bi avê.. bi tomer
lê dixistin, tê de genim dikutan.
 
Yeah... auntie says they pounded wheat in it. With water..
they hit it with a mallet, they pounded wheat in it.

288
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:45,000
Xaltîk mezin e, zane.
 
Auntie is older, she knows.

289
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,000
Berê cefa pir bû tiştê giran bû.
 
In the past, there was a lot of suffering, things were hard.

290
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Giran bû.
 
It was hard.

291
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:52,000
Erê ev alî jî malê Ehmedê Hesen ne.
 
Yes, this side is Ahmed Hasan's house.

292
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Gundîyekî mezin.
 
A prominent villager.

293
00:20:54,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Silavên me ji wan malbatê re hene, malbatên giya re, gundî
mezin re.
 
We send our greetings to that family, to all those families,
to the prominent villagers.

294
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Xaltîk te digo... ev e te tomer got, tê de dikutan bi
xelkê...
 
Auntie you were saying... this you called a mallet, they
used to pound in it with the people...

295
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Ev e genim e.. berî, xelkê ortê gund dibirîn, da genim di
kutan.
 
This is wheat.. in the past, people from the center of the
village would take it, and they pounded wheat.

296
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:12,000
Genim jî sê şeş caran lê dixistin zîwa dibûn, dibirin
dihêran.
 
They hit the wheat three or six times and it dried, then
they took it and ground it.

297
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Dan jî pê dikutan, dan jî pê dikutan, erê ev e xwe tişt ê
bes ê dan û genim e... pê dikutan.
 
They pounded grain with it too, they pounded grain with it
too, yes this is just a thing for grain and wheat... they
pounded with it.

298
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:21,000
Xaltîk, berê, berê xweştir bû lê noko xweştir e?
 
Auntie, in the past, was the past better or is now better?

299
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Weleh berê xweştir bû, rehetî nebû lê bes berê kêftir bû.
 
By God, the past was better, there was no comfort but the
past was more joyful.

300
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,000
Berê noko kêftir bû ne?
 
The past was more joyful than now, wasn't it?

301
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:34,000
Erê, erê. Xêr û bêr pir bû berê. Însan li qebûl... cîran li
qebûl... ehbab hebûn... dost...
 
Yes, yes. There were many blessings in the past. People were
accepting... neighbors were accepting... there were
friends... acquaintances...

302
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Yanî bera tirsnê, ev bera... ev bera cîranê te ye... ferq tê
nebû... ferq tê nebû, na.
 
I mean without fear, this fruit... this fruit is your
neighbor's... there was no difference... there was no
difference, no.

303
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:43,000
Wa pir cefa dîtin a xaltîk berê?
 
Did you see a lot of suffering auntie, in the past?

304
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:49,000
Weleh me xwe.. berê halek dîtin... em pir me cefa dîtin..
hal... me mêr kir hatin gund...
 
By God we... saw a situation in the past... we saw a lot of
suffering.. situation... we got married and came to the
village...

305
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

306
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:52,000
Bes de me ewana rahmetî pir cefa dîtin.
 
But then those late ones saw a lot of suffering.

307
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,000
Pir dîtin ne?
 
They saw a lot, didn't they?

308
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

309
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:58,000
Ê noko... tehm nemaye. Adem û însan... tehm û hesîyat wî
nemaye.
 
And now... there's no taste left. Man and humans... its
taste and feeling are not left.

310
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:02,000
Hesîyet... na.. erê nemaye hesîyet... dê înşelleh wê rehet
bibe tehmekî wê bibînin erê.
 
Feeling... no.. yes there's no feeling left... but God
willing it will get comfortable, they will see a taste, yes.

311
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:04,000
Înşelleh rojên xweş wê bibînin înşelleh.
 
God willing they will see good days, God willing.

312
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:10,000
Înşelleh. Hemdîlillah deh sal e em ji herbê ketin, e hatiye
minteqê xwe am vegeriyane, hemdil silametî.
 
God willing. Thank God it's been 10 years since we fell into
the war, we came to our region, we returned, thank God for
safety.

313
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:13,000
Xwedê destê xwe li ser gundîyan rabigire. Minteqa xweşbî ye.
 
May God keep his hand over the villagers. It's a good
region.

314
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:18,000
Xweş bî ye, lê minteqa xweş bî ye. Şebê me hatin in... her
tişt xweş bî ye. Inşelleh.
 
It was good, yes it was a good region. Our youth came...
everything became good. God willing.

315
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:23,000
Înşelleh gundiyên dîtir jî wira vegerin... em şebê xwe
bibînin... em derdê wan... ev a ne derd e...
 
God willing the other villagers will return here too... we
see our youth... their pain... this is not pain...

316
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:26,000
Gî werin, înşelleh kesên mayî jî gî werin.. nêzîk da gî
werin.
 
Let them all come, God willing the remaining ones will all
come too.. let them all come soon.

317
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:31,000
Înşelleh. Qewmên xwe, cîranên xwe.. erdê xwe, milkê xwe.
Baran jî xweş lê kir.
 
God willing. Their relatives, their neighbors.. their land,
their property. The rain poured down nicely too.

318
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:35,000
Na dibêjin barana rehmê, ew jî wisa wek barana rehmê ye.
 
No they say rain of mercy, they too are like a rain of
mercy.

319
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:36,000
Lê, erê.
 
Yes, yes.

320
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:41,000
O noko em çi bikin, de ha va gotê rehmê ew jî mîna Xwedê ha
hatê rehmê... baranê lê kir da derbe.
 
And now what should we do, since this is called mercy, they
too came like God's mercy... it rained so it would strike.

321
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:42,000
Erê. Xwedê xêrê bişîne.
 
Yes. May God send goodness.

322
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:47,000
Amîn. De deha pênc sal in di herbê de da der û dor.. da
xirab e... ne qolay e...
 
Amen. For fifteen years in the war, around and about.. it
was ruined... it's not easy...

323
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:49,000
Ne qolay e... tiştekî xirab e, millet herin nêşûderê kî...
îleh.
 
It's not easy... it's a bad thing, people going
everywhere... exactly.

324
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:51,000
Yavaş yavaş gî vegerin wek berê bive înşelleh.
 
Slowly slowly everyone returns, it becomes like before God
willing.

325
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:57,000
Heye ez zeytûn noj dikim, e nav lê ne, zeytûna xwe diçinin,
erdê xwe dajon...
 
Yes I am picking olives, those who are not here, they pick
their olives, they plow their land...

326
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:01,000
Yanî hewşê xwe xirab bîye, çêdikin... înşelleh ê werin.. bi
emrî Xwedê.
 
I mean their courtyard was ruined, they fix it... God
willing they will come.. by God's command.

327
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Lê we dewletên Ewrûpa û alemê we dîtiye ne? Herba alemî ya
yekê û ya diduyan dîtine.
 
But you have seen the states of Europe and the world, right?
They saw the first and second world wars.

328
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:10,000
Îcar noko bajar û gundên wan ji me rintir in ne? Ne wisa ye?
 
Now their cities and villages are better than ours, right?
Isn't it so?

329
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:11,000
Înşelleh ê çêbin. Lê, ê çêbin.
 
God willing they will be built. Yes, they will be built.

330
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:16,000
Milet ê derê û derê zîyaret.. di şixulin, em jî wisa bikin
em jî... înşelleh.
 
The people will go here and there to visit.. they are
working, we should do the same too... God willing.

331
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:17,000
Şella. Şella.
 
Hopefully. Hopefully.

332
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:20,000
Bes mirov e însan jî... hez bike înşelleh gund derbas bibe.
Heskirin berî giya.
 
But it's humans, people too... should love, God willing the
village will pass this. Love before everything.

333
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:24,000
Heskirin berî giya. Inşelleh... em jî.. em carên din jî..
Xwedê... şebî me...
 
Love before everything. God willing... we too.. another time
too.. God... our youth...

334
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:30,000
Kurmancên me evana Xwedê van li ser keve, van ser caw û erdê
xwe. Ava bes ez avê tiştî dixwazim.
 
Our Kurds, may God make them succeed, them over their places
and lands. This is just what I want.

335
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,000
Silametî.
 
Safety.

336
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:32,000
Silametî ye... inşelleh.
 
It's safety... God willing.

337
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:35,000
Inşelleh, înşelleh Xwedê destê xwe li ser gîya radigire.
Çavê gî maş dikim. Xwedê we nêxe ber destan.
 
God willing, God willing may God keep his hand over
everyone. I kiss everyone's eyes. May God not put you at
anyone's mercy.

338
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,000
Amîn, amîn, amîn, amîn.
 
Amen, amen, amen, amen.

339
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:40,000
Seheta gîya xweş. Maşallah gundê me kurmancan jî...
 
Health to everyone. Mashallah our Kurdish village too...

340
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:44,000
Maşallah her gundek ser gundîyekî re ye... ew di kevin e
gund. Ava çi? Zîyaret e?
 
Mashallah every village is connected to another... that old
village. What is this? Is it a shrine?

341
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:51,000
Av a vê re dibên zîyareta.. av e ... Pîrxazî, zîyareta
Pîrxazî.
 
This, they call it the shrine of.. this is... Pirxhazi, the
shrine of Pirxhazi.

342
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:53,000
Zîyareta Pîrxazî?
 
The shrine of Pirxhazi?

343
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:54,000
Zîyareta Pîrxazî.
 
The shrine of Pirxhazi.

344
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:56,000
Ev ji mêj e?
 
This is from long ago?

345
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:57,000
Ji mêj e ne?
 
From long ago, isn't it?

346
00:23:57,000 --> 00:24:03,000
Kevnar e. Kevnar e. Û çi tiştê jî e.. ev qebîla gund a..
milkê gund e.. teberk..
 
It's ancient. It's ancient. And whatever thing is.. this
tribe of the village.. it's the property of the village..
relic..

347
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:09,000
Teberk... xa mis de daxwî xwe xwar bibe derd e wê.. derd e
qurban.. ev zîyaret e.. we zîyareta gund e.. ev gund a tê da
e.
 
Relic... if someone bends down there, it's a pain.. pain,
dear.. this is a shrine.. the shrine of the village.. this
village is in it.

348
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:16,000
Yanî yek daxwaza xwe xwar bike, bitirse, dar bike, darê
teberkê gund, dizî bike... çi dibe?
 
I mean if someone suppresses their desire, gets scared, cuts
a tree, the relic tree of the village, steals... what
happens?

349
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:22,000
Yêk... am qenaet dikin.. qenaetê wa pê nîne... ew tiştên wê
derê ne.
 
Someone... we believe.. they don't believe.. those are
things of that place.

350
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:27,000
Noko wek ca.. me.. tişt nîn e, mesela me dibêje... ba... em
Şêx Reşîd e. qurban bim.
 
Now like.. we.. there is nothing, for example we say...
well... we are Sheikh Rashid. I'd be a sacrifice.

351
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:30,000
Ewî çi qas gund rê da...
 
How much he guided the village...

352
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:36,000
Erê. Qenaetê me pê diki pir xelk bi rojan dibe... du rojan
têne... cemaet e... qenaeta te pê hebe.
 
Yes. Our belief in it makes many people go for days... they
come for two days... it's a congregation... if you have
belief in it.

353
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:41,000
Û merivek mezin jî... berê neslên xwe de... ew bûne, cîh
bûne. Gî tarîx bû ne, em nizanin.
 
And a great man too... in the past of his generations...
they became, they became a place. They all became history,
we don't know.

354
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:46,000
Nexwe we dare pêncî sal... dused sal, sêsed sal em
nizanin... em kî bûn, kî bûn ew nizanin.
 
So you have trees from fifty years... two hundred years,
three hundred years we don't know... who we were, who they
were they don't know.

355
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:49,000
Mesela piçûkik... yekî... axê.. axayê de xweyî...
 
For example a little one... someone... earth.. owning the
earth...

356
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:54,000
Nika... deng... kalik e derxistî ye...
 
Now... sound... an old man has brought it out...

357
00:24:54,000 --> 00:25:00,000
Yekî qîçika weke vîya te nika danke... klîtek dev dexîn e...
ê klîta devê wê qîçika dixin...
 
Someone, a little girl like this you now put a grain... puts
a key in the mouth... they put the key in that little girl's
mouth...

358
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:03,000
Ew qîçika bi emrê Xwedê şora dikî...
 
That little girl speaks by God's command...

359
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:08,000
Û qîçikên ku axê dixwî, qîçik nan naxwe, tam axê û heriyê
dixwî...
 
And the little girls who eat dirt, the little girl doesn't
eat bread, eats only dirt and mud...

360
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:13,000
Ta ku teberka gund dikin devî gundî de holê bi emrê Xwedê
çêdibe.
 
Until they put the village's relic in the mouth of the
villager like this by God's command it happens.

361
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:16,000
Da ew jî tiştekî îlahî ye am nizanin, qenaet e gi qenaet e.
 
So that is also a divine thing we don't know, it's belief,
all belief.

362
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:36,000
Rast e. Tiştên wisa li pir gundan heye, em dibînin.
 
That's true. There are things like this in many villages, we
see.

363
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:59,000
Ev mal û hewşên ava ye... em berê wan yanî nêzîk dibin.
 
These are the houses and courtyards... we are getting closer
to them.

364
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:33,000
Ev gundê çiye?
 
What village is this?

365
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:34,000
Çeqela...
 
Çeqela...

366
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:35,000
Gundê me...
 
Our village...

367
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:55,000
Gundê me Çeqela.
 
Our village Çeqela.

368
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:20,000
Hewşoke... kaşt e...
 
Little courtyard... it's steep...

369
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:50,000
Weleh gî hewşên kevin in di gundê da ne.
 
By God they are all old courtyards in the village.

370
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Çîçek, çîçekê biharê no.
 
Flower, look at the spring flower.

371
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:21,000
Mêze çîçekê, te çîçekê dîtîne biharê no? Dît ye?
 
Look at the flower, have you seen the spring flowers? Did
you see?

372
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:41,000
Ma te dîtiye? çîçek? te dîtine, ha binêre.
 
Have you seen it? The flower? Have you seen it, look here.

373
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:51,000
Bi dar e, bi guhro, ba wuro.
 
Look at the tree, and the hill, look here.

374
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:54,000
Maşallah, maşallah.
 
Mashallah, mashallah.

375
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:58,000
Maşallah tu li kî derê xweş e gundê me ye gund.
 
Mashallah, our village is so beautiful wherever you go.

376
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:00,000
Ha binêrin. Kopek diyar e axo...
 
Look. A dog is visible...

377
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:02,000
Bê bê tu wuko.
 
Look over there.

378
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:08,000
Çi ecwa ye.
 
What an atmosphere.

379
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:15,000
Dinya germ e ka...
 
The weather is warm...

380
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:25,000
A rê qoltik e... em bi ser qoltikê de... ecwa wê çiqas xweş
e. Ev e qoltik e. Gundî yê me ye... we.
 
Here the road is a bend... we turn on this bend... how nice
the atmosphere is. This is a bend. Our villagers... look.

381
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:27,000
Behîv we dî çiqas hişîn bûne.
 
Did you see how green the almonds have become.

382
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:33,000
Maşallah we.
 
Mashallah to them.

383
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:37,000
Ecwa pir xweş e.
 
The atmosphere is very nice.

384
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:40,000
Erebe naxwaze tu tiştî axa na.
 
The car doesn't need anything, there is no earth/mud.

385
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:46,000
A ev malên xweş in... hewşên kevir in... darek e...
 
Look at these nice houses... stone yards... a tree...

386
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:54,000
Aha ecwa... tu kî derê tike.
 
Here is the atmosphere... wherever you look.

387
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:57,000
Gundî kî dikê.
 
The villagers built it.

388
00:31:57,000 --> 00:32:05,000
Tarî ye reşe we dî?
 
Did you see it is dark and black?

389
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:11,000
Bi darê ji, ev hewşên jor te dît ha ke... ev hewşên jor
in...
 
Look at these trees too, you saw these upper yards, right...
these are the upper yards...

390
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:15,000
Vî dera ji di wextê zilzilê çêbûya, giya çadir ava kirin...
 
Here too, when the earthquake happened, they all set up
tents...

391
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:18,000
Çadir e... ka wuro...
 
It's a tent... look here...

392
00:32:18,000 --> 00:32:20,000
Na na...
 
No no...

393
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:23,000
A na... gundiyan e. Ke, çima weha ye.
 
Oh no... it belongs to the villagers. Look, why is it like
that.

394
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:43,000
Gundiyan meşin... wuro.
 
The villagers set it up... look here.

395
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:13,000
Em hewşa kî ne...
 
Whose yard are we at...

396
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:17,000
Ev hewşê Qesîra me ne.
 
This is our Qesir's yard.

397
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:20,000
Ev hewşa Xelîl e.
 
This is Xelil's yard.

398
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:40,000
Ev avahiyên gundê me.
 
These are the buildings of our village.

399
00:33:55,000 --> 00:34:00,000
Çi hewşek rind e. Maşallah ji vî gundî rind e.
 
What a beautiful yard. Mashallah, this village is beautiful.

400
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:03,000
Ev dîwarên gundê me ne, biniyê gund e.
 
These are the walls of our village, it's below the village.

401
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:10,000
Hewşê xortan û gundiyan e.
 
It's the yard of the youth and the villagers.

402
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:29,000
Dorê çîçek vebûna, maşallah wuro.
 
Flowers have bloomed around, mashallah look here.

403
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:31,000
Aha ev vî gundî, tirbên gund e ne.
 
Look, in this village, these are the village graves.

404
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:37,000
Ew tirbên gund e... mezin in.
 
Those are the village graves... they are big.

405
00:34:37,000 --> 00:34:44,000
Mektebê gund e li xwar û jêr e...
 
The village school is down here...

406
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Bes mekteb firn e... ne şixul e ev e xirab bûye.
 
But the school is not working, it is ruined.

407
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:52,000
Mekteb car din da bi gundiyan re vebîne.
 
The school should be opened for the villagers again.

408
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:55,000
Aha.
 
Look.

409
00:34:55,000 --> 00:35:15,000
Ser vê rê meşkin... islah kirine... bes da bi gundiyan re...
xwendegeh çêbibe... mekteb xirab dibe... mekteb jî car din
da bibîne...
 
Look at this road... they repaired it... but a school should
be built in the village for the villagers... the school gets
ruined... the school should be seen again...

410
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:23,000
Vî dera jî... meqbez e... meqbeza zeytûna.
 
Here too... it's a press... an olive press.

411
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:25,000
Akîd belê meqbeza...
 
Surely yes, it's a press...

412
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:28,000
Eh meqbeza zeytûna.
 
Yes, an olive press.

413
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:34,000
Meqbeza zeytûna yê me.
 
Our olive press.

414
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Erê vî derê jî, çêlek çêdikin. Min xalê pirs kir, min got
"Ev makbez a?". Got "Na makbez nîne, ev ciya çêlo ye."
Mezreayê çêlan ava kirin da.
 
Yes, here too, they keep cows. I asked my uncle, I said "Is
this a press?". He said "No, it's not a press, it's a place
for cows." They built a cow farm.

415
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:45,000
Seetê gundî xweş se ke. Meşrû'a ev, meşrû'a nacih e...
 
May the villagers' time be good, look. This project is a
successful project...

416
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:49,000
Mîye bi mîye nacih e.
 
A hundred percent successful.

417
00:35:49,000 --> 00:35:56,000
Wele min dît mezin çêkirine, min got zor kiye, meqbeza
zeytûnê dera ye. Dê xalî dibê mezreçêlo ye.
 
By God, I saw they built it big, I said it must be a big
olive press. The uncle says it's a cow farm.

418
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:58,000
Rind e, rind e. Xwedê ristiqê gundiyan bişîne.
 
It's good, it's good. May God send the villagers their
livelihood.

419
00:35:58,000 --> 00:36:01,000
Sehetê te xweş xalo.
 
May your time be good, uncle.

420
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Tim we, Xwedê ristiqê gund bide, tiştê rind e rind e. Em
kêfxweş dibin.
 
Always like this, may God give the village its livelihood,
it's a good thing. We get happy.

421
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:10,000
Erê evên vî dera jî, me gundê mezin xelas kir teswîr...
 
Yes, these here too, we finished filming the big village...

422
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:13,000
Em ê herin mal dar e...
 
We will head towards home...

423
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:16,000
Erê... silavê min ji miletê gund re ya na.
 
Yes... my greetings to the people of the village.

424
00:36:16,000 --> 00:36:18,000
Çavê gundiyan maç dikim, Xwedê gund bixwefîne.
 
I kiss the eyes of the villagers, may God protect the
village.

425
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:21,000
Xalê jî, yê mezreçêlo çêdike... sehetê wî jî xweş...
 
The uncle too, who is building the cow farm... may his time
be good too...

426
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:24,000
Çavê wî jî maç dikim. Xwedê rizqê wî zêde bike.
 
I kiss his eyes too. May God increase his livelihood.

427
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:31,000
Gundekî pir xweş e, kîbar a... ev jî û gundê jorî jî me
sawirandin, gundin pir xweş kîbar in.
 
It's a very nice village, cute... this and the upper village
too we filmed, they are very nice and cute villages.

428
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:33,000
Miletî tê de jî kîbar in a, rind in a.
 
The people in it are also nice, they are good.

429
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:36,000
Bi mera bin vîdyoyên din xweş kîbar, em ê wera çêkin
inşallah nêzîk de em ê daxin.
 
Stay with us for other nice and cute videos, we will make
them for you inshallah, we will upload them soon.

430
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:42,000
Ka farde li jor in, û ev jêr in... em ê bi sawirînin naqle
pêşeroj înşallah.
 
Look at those above, and these below... we will film them in
the future inshallah.

431
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:48,000
Erê bi mera bin xelqê din xweş em ê we re çêkin, qisûrî me
e'fû bikin, îze şaşbûnek tê de hebîn, qisûr e efû bikin.
 
Yes, stay with us, other nice people, we will make for you,
forgive our shortcomings, if there was any mistake in it,
forgive the shortcoming.

432
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Neşta teswîrê me ev ha wina ye, vîdyoyê me ekseriye xwar e
we fê ne...
 
Our filming capability is just like this, our videos are
mostly down and up like this...

433
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:53,000
Lû'ey min, te ke şore ne xwe bike.
 
My Lu'ey, you say a word too for yourself.

434
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:55,000
Layk û iştîrakê me ra lê xin.
 
Put a like and subscribe for us.

435
00:36:55,000 --> 00:36:58,000
Işt ho. Layk û iştîrakê ji Lû'ey min re lê xin ho.
 
That's it. Put a like and subscribe for my Lu'ey.

436
00:36:58,000 --> 00:37:01,000
Sehetê we xweş... dibe bi mera bin... gelek ecwa pir xweş e.
 
May your time be good... stay with us... there's a lot of
very nice atmosphere.

437
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:06,000
Bahar e, dîdar e, ciyên wekî nokî şîn bîne, xelkî milkê xwe
cût kir...
 
It's spring, it's visible, places like chickpea fields have
become green, people plowed their property...

438
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:11,000
Darên behîvê giş hişîn bûne, qurt û behîv, gî kulîlk jê
dertên...
 
Almond trees have all become green, wolves and almonds, all
flowers are blooming from them...

439
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:16,000
Seheta giya xweş be be mera bin, vîdyoyên xweş, kîbar em we
re daxin. Bay bay. Do'a bikin, do'a bikin.
 
May everyone's time be good, stay with us, we will upload
nice, cute videos for you. Bye bye. Pray, pray.

